===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{informal|mainly|British|dated in US}} A [[male]] person.
#* '''1922''', [[w:P. G. Wodehouse|P. G. Wodehouse]], ''Right Ho, Jeeves'', ch. 19,
#*: You are a silly young '''geezer'''.
# {{informal|mainly|US|sometimes|mildly|derogatory}} An [[old]] person, usually a male.
#* '''2000''', Moira McDonald, "[http://community.seattletimes.nwsource.com/archive/?date=20000825&slug=4038797 Outakes]," ''Seattle Times'', 25 Aug. (retrieved 6 Sep. 2008),
#*: The technical term for a female '''geezer''' is "old broad," but this is irrelevant, as nobody in Hollywood makes films about women over 55.
# {{British}} A device for [[boil]]ing water for such [[domestic]] uses as heating or washing; a [[boiler]]. The normal spelling is water {{term|geyser}} - for the obvious reason!

